  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WASH IM Officer with UNICEF Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is an assignment at the request of UNICEF. Zimbabwe is experiencing a cholera outbreak since February 2023, which has been spiking particularly since mid-October. The UNICEF Zimbabwe WASH team is covering the overall coordination and UNICEF&#x2019;s response. However, information management (IM) remains a major weakness. This is in part due to the fact that the last major cholera outbreak was in 2019 when government emergency management systems were stronger in the WASH sector. Even in 2019, UNICEF had a dedicated Emergency IM Specialist during that outbreak.In order to strengthen IM efforts, including rapid collection, analysis and presentation of data as well as to strengthen provincial and district authorities to improve information management and reporting, a dedicated Standby Partner expert is requested for a period of three months.</narrative>
  </description>
